# Generated by `make web`: a byte-for-byte copy of the production assets from
# ../uap-web and the ../uap-js library they import, staged here only so
# //go:embed web/* can pull them into the binary. Committing it would fork the
# frontend into a second copy that silently drifts. `make web` (which `make
# build` and `make check-web` both depend on) regenerates it -- note that
# `go build`/`go test` here fail after `make clean` until it has been run,
# because //go:embed web/* needs at least one matching file.
web/

# Build output
uap-indexer
uap-indexer-stripped
uap-indexer.upx

# The repository root's .gitignore carries an autotools-era `Makefile` rule --
# every Makefile in this tree is generated by ./configure from a Makefile.am,
# so ignoring the name wholesale is right for the C++ side. This one is not
# generated; it is hand-written and is the only thing that knows how to build
# web/ before //go:embed can see it. Without this re-inclusion the file is
# invisible to git, a fresh clone has no Makefile here, and `make web` -- and
# therefore every `go build`/`go test`/CI job in this directory -- fails.
!Makefile
